{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And YHWH spoke to Moses, saying, etc. — When a man makes a singular vow</b>. This passage too is attached, for it was at Mount Sinai joined to the admonitions, since it deals with the laws of the Jubilee, as he mentioned in connection with one who dedicates a purchased field (below, verses 23–24) and an inherited field (ibid., 17–18), except that he included the laws of all vows in a single passage. Therefore he said at the end: \"These are the commandments that YHWH commanded Moses to the children of Israel at Mount Sinai\" (Leviticus 27:34), concerning all that was stated above, for from here onward he will speak of the commandments of the Tent of Meeting:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:01:22.273684374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}